    Notes:
	- These are hardcoded because the site structure rarely changes.
    - Only the indexable pages are listed. The following aren't listed:
      - /search/ results are noindex
	  - /search/random/ is a redirect
      - /admin/ pages are noindex
	  - /api is disallowed in robots.txt
	- The lastmod is omitted for /search/browse/ and /search/new/
	  because they are dynamically generated and the content changes 
	  several times a day. The lastmod for the other pages should
	  be manually updated when changes are made to those pages.
	- The browse pages are listed individually because they contain 
	  unique content (site home pages) which we want search engines to 
	  index, but which search engines won't be able to find because the 
	  normal browse navigation is via POST. The canonical URL for these
	  has to be updated to include the allowed params otherwise search 
	  engines will skip as duplicates. In theory we should go up to
	  (currently) page 198 (3955 sites / 20 site per page) but I 
	  don't want to use up the crawl budget on browse.
	 -->
